    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Maurya Empire, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pataliputra">Pataliputra</a>, was the first state to unite almost the whole Indian subcontinent.</li><li>Its centralised administration and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ashoka">Ashoka</a>'s edicts promoting dhamma helped carry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#buddhism">Buddhism</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia">Asia</a>.</li><li>It fell apart after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ashoka">Ashoka</a>'s death and ended c. 185 BCE when Pushyamitra Shunga killed the last emperor, Brihadratha.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ashoka">Ashoka</a>'s Lion Capital from Sarnath, carved from polished sandstone over 2,000 years ago, is today the national emblem of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#india">India</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

